+- It never sends, clicks or calls a site for you. You always start the send yourself.
+- Text you paste is masked as it lands.
+- **Autopilot** is on by default. While you type, after a short pause (about 0.4 seconds), the TDS extension masks what it finds in the chat box: finished words only, and only when the cursor is at the end of the text. When you leave the chat box, it masks all of it. When you send, it masks what is left, checks the box again, and then lets your send go on. If it cannot mask the text or cannot read the box, it stops the send and tells you.
+- **Typed text is still unmasked in the chat box for a short time, and the site's page can read the box in that time.** That is: until the pause after a finished word, or until you leave the box or send. The word you are typing, and text typed with the cursor not at the end, stay unmasked until the pause at the end, until you leave the box, or until you send.
+- You can switch Autopilot off in the menu; your organisation can set the default and lock it. With Autopilot off, typed text is checked when you press Enter or Send, or Alt+Shift+M, and sits unmasked in the chat box until then.
